From: jayneelatintel <jayneel.vora@intel.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 22:46:10 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 12/21] dist-tp: opt-in multi-chunk ND messages
 (LLAMA_DIST_TP_RDMA_MULTICHUNK)

A receiver acks only while it consumes, inside nd_recv_raw. When both
ends of a link send a message longer than the 23-chunk window before
either receives, which is every full-duplex exchange and the edge an
odd ring cannot 2-colour, both block at the window waiting for an ack
neither will send. That is why payloads above one 256 KiB chunk had to
stay on TCP, and why the prompt only stayed on RDMA with a small -ub.

With LLAMA_DIST_TP_RDMA_MULTICHUNK=1 a sender blocked at its window
keeps receiving: it takes every arrived chunk off the receive ring of
every live connection into a per-connection side buffer, reposts the
receive and acks once per window, as nd_recv_raw would have. A message
may then span any number of chunks, so a full prompt batch rides RDMA.

- Acks posted while blocked leave from a dedicated 64-byte slot after
  the tx ring (same registered buffer), because the blocked sender's
  ring slot holds a staged data chunk. They complete under their own
  context and at most one is in flight per direction, as before.
- nd_recv_raw reads the side buffer before rx_ready. Only bytes that
  arrived after the side buffer's are in rx_ready, so order is kept.
- With one connection (2 ranks) the blocked sender waits on its CQ as
  before. With several (3-rank ring or mesh) no single CQ can be slept
  on, so it polls them in turn and checks the ring sockets for a
  vanished peer once per liveness tick.
- The completion error report moves into nd_completion_ok, the routing
  half of nd_step becomes nd_route, and nd_try_step consumes one
  completion if one is ready.

Unset, the window wait is unchanged. The ceiling on what goes over RDMA
is still LLAMA_DIST_TP_RDMA_MAX_BYTES; set it to 0 to send every
payload over RDMA. The first time a sender waits at its window with the
mode on, the rank prints
"[dist-tp][nd] multi-chunk messages: a blocked sender keeps receiving".
